==English==
===Verb===
'''[[cop]] [[out]]'''
#{{idiom}} To [[avoid]] or [[shirk]], either by failing to perform, or by performing in a grossly [[insufficient]], [[negligent]], or [[superficial]] manner.
#:''Faced with the prospect of cooking for himself, his first thought was to '''cop out''' and order a pizza.''
#:''Faced with electric eel checkout, one is inclinded to feign a scaff bay stocktake, often using an old clip board to enhance the illusion of responsibility. Alternative options include such measures as the backroom copout, or the 2 ton tabtop copout''
#:'' common names associated with the term copout include, WILLIAM "shirk" Fisher a.k.a electric eel specialist and vintage eel historian/enthusiast.''

